<LegalPage
  title="About SpotAI · who builds it and why"
  description="SpotAI is built by Yaseen Khatib in Hyderabad: a gym app for members and a management console for gym owners in India. What it is, what is real today and how to reach me."
  heading="About SpotAI"
>
  <p class="lead">
    SpotAI is a gym app for India, built and run by one person: <a href={SITE.author.url} rel="author">{SITE.author.name}</a>, a
    full-stack software engineer based in Hyderabad, Telangana.
  </p>

  <h2>What SpotAI is</h2>
  <p>
    It has two sides. Members get an app with today's workout, a gym leaderboard, workout buddies and an AI coach that checks
    squat form on the phone camera: knees caving in, shallow depth and forward lean, rep by rep. The camera video stays on the
    phone. Gym owners get a console that shows who came in, who stopped coming and who owes a fee, plus a front-desk view that
    checks members in by QR code or by name without anyone installing an app.
  </p>

  <h2>Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    Many small gyms in India run on a paper register and WhatsApp reminders. Fees are chased by hand, nobody notices a member
    who quietly stops coming, and new lifters get no feedback on form. SpotAI is an attempt to give those gyms visibility
    at a price a one-room gym can afford, in the languages their members speak: the app is available in English, Hindi,
    Telugu, Tamil, Kannada, Marathi and Bengali.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it stands today</h2>
  <p>
    SpotAI is an early product. You can try the full member app today as an offline demo build (Android, iPhone or in the
    browser; what you save stays on your phone). The first {SITE.pilot.gyms} gyms in India get a free {SITE.pilot.days}-day pilot,
    set up remotely over a video call and WhatsApp, and in person around Hyderabad. Pricing after the pilot has not been
    announced, and this site does not publish customer numbers, testimonials or results, because there are none to show yet.
  </p>

  <h2>The guides on this site</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/guides/">guides</a> are written for gym members and gym owners: food calories and protein from published USDA
    and ICMR-NIN tables, workout and form explanations, and practical notes for running a gym. Where a guide gives a number it
    says where the number comes from. Some are translated into Indian languages; those translations are reviewed before they
    are listed in search. If you find a mistake, email me and I will fix it.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or see the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. My other work is at
    <a href={SITE.author.url}>{SITE.author.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
